From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominik Weber <doweb85@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:18:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/27] byteplan: keep the start of new chats on the SSD
 (BYTEPLAN_PROMPT_DISK)

The state at the first user message (system prompt + tool definitions) of the main and the MTP
context is written to files once, together with the protected checkpoint of patch 0011. After a
server restart, a new chat or agent session with the same start loads it (0.1 s) instead of
reading it again (33 s for 13.6k tokens). Entries are keyed by model files, build, batch and
context sizes, KV types and Byteplan settings; BYTEPLAN_PROMPT_DISK_GB (default 8) caps the folder,
least recently used first. The loaded state is the saved one bit for bit, and the prompt continues
at the same batch boundary, so answers are unchanged.
---
 tools/server/server-context.cpp | 273 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tools/server/server-models.cpp  |   2 +-
 tools/server/server-models.h    |   5 +
 3 files changed, 279 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

